# Phase 18 P18-V01 — Fastjson empty-value writer features

- Timestamp: 2026-10-16 22:56:47 UTC
- Branch: `phase/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate`
- Code commit: `dc791e63` (`feat(protocol): support empty writer features`)
- Java oracle: RocketMQ client 5.5.1; Fastjson2 2.0.63 fixtures already pinned
- Scope: implement the fixture-observed `NotWriteEmptyArray` and `IgnoreEmpty`
  writer behaviors across inherited body, route, and heartbeat serializers.

## Changes

- Empty arrays/collections and empty maps are omitted from object properties by
  `NotWriteEmptyArray`; `IgnoreEmpty` also omits empty-string properties.
- The feature validation accepts both options, and fixture comparisons cover
  default, populated, nested, body, route, and heartbeat DTO cases where the
  pinned Java output differs.
- The Phase 6 map now records eight behavior-mapped writer features out of 48;
  the remaining 40 are still explicitly unsupported.

## Validation

- `TZ=UTC cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-protocol --all-features --locked`:
  passed (122 unit tests, all Protocol integration targets, 42 doctests).
- `cargo clippy -p rocketmq-classic-protocol --all-targets --all-features
  --locked -- -D warnings`: passed.
- `TZ=UTC mvn -o -q -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify`: passed all 37
  scenarios and Java/Rust fixture-drift checks.
- `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check`: passed.
- Full workspace default and all-feature tests passed on parent revision
  `c7c26cc0`; the final full-workspace P18-V02 gate is still required after
  `dc791e63`.

